{"id":"edge-over-time","title":"Does the edge persist or come and go?","question":"For the consistently faster firms, is the edge there every year, and does it begin or end at a recognisable date?","finding":"The edge is mostly a standing feature of the firm, not an episode. Taking the 60 consistently faster firms together, they beat like permits on 65% of jobs filed through 2019, 63% in 2020 and 2021, and 66% from 2022. Of the 51 named, 38 held the edge on both sides of the 2020 and 2021 cases, 3 saw it fade afterwards, 0 saw it grow, 3 had stopped filing by 2022 and 7 have too few jobs on one side to say. Across all 346 tested firms with at least 20 jobs in both periods, the share faster before 2020 and the share faster from 2022 move together (correlation 0.54): 49 of the 61 firms that beat like permits on more than 60% of jobs before 2020 still beat them on more than half afterwards.","how":"For each firm in the first screen, the share of its jobs faster than the like-permit median in four periods of filing years: 2012 to 2015, 2016 to 2019, 2020 and 2021, and 2022 to 2024 (a period with fewer than 8 jobs is left blank). The change column is the share from 2022 minus the share through 2019. An edge is called faded when the later share is one half or less, or fell by 15 points or more and by more than 2.5 standard errors; grown is the mirror image. The dates set beside each firm are its first filing on the Ethics Commission's permit-consultant register and the issue date of its State contractor licence, where either exists. The dates of the cases come from the case file: 2020-03-11, Building Inspection director Tom Hui resigns after the City Attorney's findings; 2020-05-12, Santos is charged with bank fraud; 2021-08-20, Curran and Santos are charged over the donations scheme. Ordinance 93-23, enacted 2023-05-26, requires applications to be processed in the order received.","limits":"Firms were picked because they were fast over the whole period, so some drift back toward the middle in any later slice is expected by arithmetic alone and is not evidence that anything changed. Filings fell sharply in 2020 and the mix of work changed, which moves the cells as well as the firms. A firm that stops filing may have closed, merged or changed its name; the permit records do not say which, and ownership changes are not recorded in any file used here. A persistent edge fits a specialty or a well-run office at least as well as it fits favour.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"firm","t":"Firm or licensed professional","type":"org"},{"k":"role","t":"Listed on permits as","type":"text"},{"k":"jobs","t":"Jobs compared","type":"int"},{"k":"p1","t":"Share faster, 2012 to 2015","type":"pct"},{"k":"p2","t":"2016 to 2019","type":"pct"},{"k":"p3","t":"2020 and 2021","type":"pct"},{"k":"p4","t":"2022 to 2024","type":"pct"},{"k":"change","t":"Change after 2021","type":"pct"},{"k":"verdict","t":"Reading","type":"text"},{"k":"dates","t":"Dates on record","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"firm":"Siemens Industry, Inc.","firmKey":null,"role":"Contractor","jobs":1992,"p1":0.526,"p2":0.533,"p3":0.573,"p4":0.617,"change":0.087,"verdict":"Edge held before and after","dates":"State contractor licence 758796 issued 02/04/1999"},{"firm":"Skyline Construction","firmKey":null,"role":"Contractor","jobs":1609,"p1":0.605,"p2":0.614,"p3":0.54,"p4":0.447,"change":-0.163,"verdict":"Edge faded after 2021","dates":"State contractor licence 727637 issued 09/17/1996"},{"firm":"Novo Construction Inc","firmKey":null,"role":"Contractor","jobs":1552,"p1":0.527,"p2":0.674,"p3":0.719,"p4":0.633,"change":0.027,"verdict":"Edge held before and after","dates":"State contractor licence 791022 issued 02/06/2001"},{"firm":"BCCI Construction Company","firmKey":null,"role":"Contractor","jobs":1431,"p1":0.786,"p2":0.76,"p3":0.615,"p4":0.657,"change":-0.115,"verdict":"Edge held before and after","dates":"State contractor licence 492944 issued 06/05/1986"},{"firm":"GCI, Inc","firmKey":null,"role